<title>JAPAN: Nichimen says to buy back 2.08 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Nichimen says to buy back 2.08 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading house Nichimen Corp said on Wednesday that it would offer to repurchase 2.08 million of its shares at 400 yen per share.  </p>
<p>Nichimen said in a statement that the move to buy back its shares, which will be carried out between July 10 and July 30, was tied to a decision approved at a recent shareholders' meeting to adopt a stock option plan for Nichimen executives.</p>
<p>It said that it would spend 867 million yen to buy the shares, including costs from brokerage commissions.</p>
</text>
